From: Roman Senn <roman.l.senn@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] service: a half-closed wsi has no parked rx to consume

A server that answers before reading the request body (eg a POST handler
that responds straight from the HTTP callback with Connection: close) ends
up half-closed (LCS_SHUTDOWN), waiting for the peer FIN, with the unread
body still on its buflist. lws_wsi_can_consume_parked_rx() kept saying that
buflist could be consumed, so lws_service_adjust_timeout() returned 0
forever and an external-poll loop (qjs-lws) spun inside one service pass,
starving every other wsi - including the client waiting for that response.

Made against libwebsockets 222ccba9f (main).

---
diff --git a/lib/io/service.c b/lib/io/service.c
index 732d27001..9825f6243 100644
--- a/lib/io/service.c
+++ b/lib/io/service.c
@@ -324,6 +324,15 @@ lws_wsi_can_consume_parked_rx(struct lws *wsi)
 	if (lws_is_flowcontrolled(wsi))
 		return 0;
 
+	/*
+	 * Half-closed, waiting only for the peer's FIN: whatever is parked
+	 * (eg an unread request body the response did not wait for) will
+	 * never be consumed, so offering it for service again would just
+	 * spin the event loop until the peer finally closes
+	 */
+	if (lwsi_close(wsi) == LCS_SHUTDOWN)
+		return 0;
+
 	switch (lwsi_state(wsi)) {
 	case LRS_TXN_COMPLETED:
 	case LRS_TXN_COMPLETING:
